secubox-antirootkit (0.1.1-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=high

  * Retire `RuntimeDirectory=secubox` (ref #1022). Ce repertoire est PARTAGE par
    une centaine de modules ; `RuntimeDirectory=` est concu pour un repertoire
    PROPRE a un service. systemd le recreait a chaque demarrage avec le mode de
    l'unite : le dernier demarre imposait le sien, et huit unites le posaient en
    0755 — privant tous les autres du droit d'y creer leur socket. Le meme
    mecanisme l'effacait a l'arret d'un service, emportant les sockets des
    quatre-vingt-dix autres. Il est desormais declare une seule fois, en 1777,
    par le tmpfiles.d de secubox-core.

 -- Gerald Kerma <devel@cybermind.fr>  Thu, 13 Aug 2026 11:00:00 +0200

secubox-antirootkit (0.1.0-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: anti-rootkit host-IDS (ref #915).
    - Anti-escape (LIVE): sbx-untrusted.slice (top-level cgroup) + nft
      secubox_antiescape table drops all egress from jailed processes
      except lan_safe destinations (socket cgroupv2 level 1 match); the
      nft ruleset is now idempotent (add+delete+redefine) so reloading it
      never appends duplicate rules.
    - Exec scanner (LIVE): auditd targeted watches (/usr/local/bin,
      /usr/local/sbin, /tmp, /dev/shm, /opt, /usr/lib/jvm, /home, key
      sbx_exec) feed api/execwatch.py via a real polling cursor (each
      audit record is processed exactly once, never re-jailed/re-logged
      on overlapping ausearch windows); unknown/non-dpkg-backed execs are
      jailed via secubox-antirootkitctl (scoped sudoers, exact-path
      NOPASSWD) and appended to the append-only exec forensic log.
    - Alerts (LIVE, alert-only): the daemon records an alert in a
      SQLite-backed store (/var/lib/secubox/antirootkit/alerts.db)
      whenever it jails a process; GET /alerts, served by the separate
      API process, returns it. Quarantine stays alert-only: POST /quarantine-prep
      never executes chmod/cp/nft/systemctl itself, it only returns an
      operator-reviewable plan (api/quarantine.py).
    - Integrity wrap (SCAFFOLDED, v1.1 follow-up): debsums/aide/rkhunter/
      chkrootkit wrappers exist in api/integrity.py and are Recommends,
      but no timer schedules them yet in this release — do not assume
      automatic integrity scanning is running.
    - FastAPI dashboard on its own /run/secubox/antirootkit.sock (no
      aggregator dependency); web panel at /antirootkit/.
    - Packaging: postinst creates the secubox-antirootkit system user,
      installs -d (never chown) the shared /var/lib/secubox parent, loads
      the nft table and audit rules, and starts sbx-untrusted.slice at
      the cgroup root (not nested under system.slice, so the nft
      `cgroupv2 level 1` match holds). Depends now includes sudo and
      nftables (the jail path and the anti-escape rely on them and would
      otherwise silently no-op if absent).

 -- Gérald Kerma <devel@cybermind.fr>  Mon, 28 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0200
